<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 26 November, from 1778 to 1965.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/james-cook" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-cook.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1778">1778 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">248 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Captain Cook sights Maui on his return to Hawaii</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On his second visit to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaiian Islands</a>, which he called the Sandwich Islands, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-cook">James Cook</a> sighted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maui">Maui</a>. He was killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kealakekua-bay">Kealakekua Bay</a> on Hawaii Island less than three months later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1789">1789 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The United States observes a national day of Thanksgiving</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> observed a national day of Thanksgiving, proclaimed by President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> at the request of Congress to encourage national unity. The new Congress had first met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> that March.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-congress">United States Congress</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1812">1812 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon's retreating army begins crossing the Berezina</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Retreating from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-armee">Grande Armée</a> began fighting its way across the Berezina River, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a>, under attack by Russian forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-wittgenstein">Wittgenstein</a> and Chichagov. Engineers bridged the river under fire, and much of the army escaped.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-berezina">Battle of the Berezina</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Podgorica Assembly votes for Montenegro's union with Serbia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/podgorica-assembly">Podgorica Assembly</a> deposed King Nicholas I and the Petrović-Njegoš dynasty of Montenegro and voted for unconditional union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, days before the creation of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a>. Opponents considered it illegitimate, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christmas-uprising">Christmas Uprising</a> followed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/podgorica-assembly">Podgorica Assembly</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1922">1922 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">104 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Howard Carter looks into Tutankhamun's tomb</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Howard Carter made a small hole in the sealed doorway and peered in by candlelight. Asked if he could see anything, he reportedly replied, 'Yes, wonderful things.'</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Red Army shells Mainila to create a pretext for war</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> shelled the Soviet border village of Mainila near Beloostrov, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> claimed that the fire came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>. The false flag operation gave it a casus belli for launching the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winter-war">Winter War</a> four days later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winter-war">Winter War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1942">1942 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Casablanca premieres in New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casablanca">Casablanca</a>, starring Humphrey Bogart and Ingrid Bergman, premiered at the Hollywood <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a> weeks after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> landed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. It won three Academy Awards, including Best Picture.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1965">1965 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France launches its first satellite</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A French Diamant rocket launched the satellite Astérix from Hammaguir in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> became the third country, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, to put a satellite into orbit on its own rocket.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a></div></div></li></ol>
